   "answer": "Based on the synthetic accessibility (SA) score tool, the SA scores for paracetamol and ibuprofen are as follows:\n\n| Molecule | Handle | Formula | SA Score | Label |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Paracetamol | `CC(=O)Nc1ccc(O)cc1` | C8H9NO2 | 1.41 | easy |\n| Ibuprofen | `CC(C)Cc1ccc(C(C)C(=O)O)cc1` | C13H18O2 | 2.19 | easy |\n\nIbuprofen (`CC(C)Cc1ccc(C(C)C(=O)O)cc1`) has a higher synthetic accessibility score (2.19) compared to paracetamol (`CC(=O)Nc1ccc(O)cc1`), which has an SA score of 1.41. Both molecules are considered easy to synthesize according to these heuristic scores."
